import PageShell from '../../../components/PageShell.astro';
import { docLinks } from '../../../data/doc-links';
---

<PageShell title="Scholarship of Application">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Furthermore, my scholarship allows me to apply my expertise in Biology education and online pedagogy
      to address institutional, student, and faculty needs. I lead the development and revision of online
      Biology courses, work with Biology faculty and Course Developers to align online courses with
      departmental learning outcomes, and collaborate with Instructional Designers and external third
      parties, such as publishers or lab providers, to maximize the quality and functionality of online
      learning experiences.
    </p>
    <p>
      One example of this work was the development of a <a href={docLinks.courseConsultant} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Course Consultant</a> model that enabled on-ground
      Biology faculty to contribute discipline-specific expertise to online course development without
      assuming responsibility for the entire development process. I also developed a <a href={docLinks.courseDevelopmentGuideline} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Course Development
      Guideline and Checklist</a> and a <a href={docLinks.courseDevelopmentTracking} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Course Development Tracking</a> system in response to recurring challenges
      identified during course development. These resources were designed to improve communication,
      clarify expectations, and support consistent course development across multiple simultaneous
      projects.
    </p>
    <p>
      This course design model has also extended beyond Biology. After discussing the approach with
      colleagues in Health Sciences and Health and Human Performance, I began supporting the redesign of
      HSI 212, HHP 345, and HHP 209. I also identified a gap in Doane's online Biology curriculum and
      worked with the Biology Chair to develop an online Ecology course.
    </p>
    <p>
      My competency in online scholarship and pedagogy led to the development of the Post-Baccalaureate
      Pre-Health Certificate. I co-developed a flexible certificate model intended to support students
      completing prerequisite and academic preparation for health-professional programs. This work
      represents an emerging area of my scholarly application as I explore how online curriculum can be
      structured to meet the needs of nontraditional and post-baccalaureate learners.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageShell>
